WEBVTT

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.700
"National Qualifier!"

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.370
I'm sorry, Takezo... for not being able
to get us a ticket to nationals.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.410
I already know.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.910
Since that day...

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.870
It's been a whole year...

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.580
"#22    Morning of the Showdown"
Good morning!

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.370
"#22    Morning of the Showdown"
Oh, good morning!

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.120
Breakfast looks like quite the feast today.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.330
Today's the national qualifier, right?
You need to get fired up!

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.660
I'll come hear your performance.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:27.500
What?!

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.290
What, you don't want me to?

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.540
Well, it's not like that, but...

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:36.080
I know you've been working hard from
early in the morning till late at night,

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.750
and yet, I've never heard
your performance, you know.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.120
I'll come with your dad to root for you.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.370
Dad, too?!

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.330
I'm glad that the qualifier is on a Sunday.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.120
I don't have any plans today,
but I'm not going.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.660
Hey, Takeru!

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:56.040
But if by some chance you guys make it
to nationals, I guess I could go.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.330
Thanks, Takeru.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.620
Kurusu?!

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.500
What're you doing here?
Did something happen?

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.330
Today we're meeting up at
the station near the venue, right?

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.040
Um... Well...

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.410
If you don't mind... um...
can we go together today?

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:22.330
I'm so nervous I feel like I'll end up
getting on the wrong train.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.910
Hold on a sec.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:26.910
You can have this.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.580
Hey, your hands!

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.250
They're very cold! How long did you wait?!

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:33.790
I-I didn't wait that long, really!

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:37.330
Hm...? Aren't your hands cold, too?

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:42.620
To tell you the truth, I've also
been nervous since yesterday...

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:47.790
So I'm a little relieved now since you're here.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.950
Let's go.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.870
Chika. You got everything?
Do you have your plectrums with you?

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:57.790
Who'd forget their plectrums
when they're going to perform?

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.000
More people than you might think.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.500
Oh. I'll come hear your performance
with Takaoka today.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.870
What? With Tetsuki? Why?

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.620
Well, I heard he was coming, too,

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.500
so I thought I'd give him a ride... by force.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.750
Are you trying to kill him?

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:16.450
See you later.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:17.580
Chika!

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.790
Snatch that ticket to nationals!

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.450
Of course we will, dummy!

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.870
"Kao School"

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.450
The award goes to...

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:42.660
...Kanagawa Prefectural...

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.290
...Hakuto High School.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.290
Kazusa seems unusually nervous.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.580
What's the matter, Nene?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.910
Listen! You'll be number one!

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:03.830
What?

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.750
Ask me "why?"!

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.580
Wh-Why?

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.450
'Cause <i>I'm </i>rooting for you!

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.000
You're such an angel! Thanks, Nene!

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:20.500
There's no way I'm gonna lose.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.660
I'm gonna take you to nationals for sure!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:29.750
That's right, Kazusa.
We, Himesaka, will never lose again.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:36.080
Jeez, Mio! The bus is already at school!

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.120
It's still not...

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.000
What?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.200
It's still not enough.
Power... I need to charge it.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.870
Mio!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:48.410
Hey! Suzumori!
So you found Kanzaki, huh? Good!

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:51.870
Mr. Yamamoto! But Mio says
he still isn't coming yet.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.200
What? Why?

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.950
Photosynthesis.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:00.370
Oh, I see! Photosynthesis, huh?
That sounds good! I'll do it, too.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.410
Whoa! This feels good, Kanzaki!

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.700
You look like you're having fun again today.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.700
Yep! I'm having fun!

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:13.660
Because the national qualifier
is finally here today!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:18.540
I've been excited for months now!

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.040
That's something.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:25.160
I couldn't go to the traditional music festival
because I got the flu, right?

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.370
Oh, yeah?

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.620
You don't remember?!

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.370
But seriously...

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:35.160
Thanks... for following me all this way.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.830
I didn't really follow you, though.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:39.910
What?!

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:43.160
Right, of course!

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.250
Whoa... I feel embarrassed.
Forget what I just said!

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.620
Mr. Yamamoto! Mio! We'll be late!

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.080
Oh... Sorry, Suzumori!

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.080
Now, get up, Kanzaki. Let's go!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.790
Listen, Mio... The fact is, Mr. Yamamoto is...

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.790
Kanzaki!

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:07.700
Hurry up, or I'll carry you to the bus!

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.000
Yeah, that's fine. Carry me on your back.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.040
What?

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.120
"Yamawa Station"

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:20.290
Okay, guys. We need to take a deep breath.
I heard exhaling is important.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:29.290
It's not working! I can't calm down at all!
My heart is about to pop out of my ear!

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.500
Oh, no! Put it back!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.160
Calm down! We can try acupressure!

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.950
My mom said pressing here on
our hands relieves tension.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:38.700
I also saw on the Internet that it
helps if we admit we're nervous!

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:41.910
Okay, let's do both! We're nervous!

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.790
What're you guys doing?

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:48.040
Ch-Ch-Ch-Ch-Ch-Chika! Hozuki!
Don't scare us like that!

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.790
Hey, why are you already so nervous?

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.080
This isn't even our first competition.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.120
That's exactly why we're more nervous!

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.660
On top of that, today... you know... um...

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.450
We can't fail... for sure...

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.330
If you're thinking like that,
you're gonna mess up.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:14.000
Hey, you should give them
a little bit of hope.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.950
It's shock therapy.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:24.040
Is your mom coming to hear
our performance today?

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:27.330
No.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.290
I sent her a letter and
mentioned today's competition,

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:33.200
but she didn't write back or call me.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.040
I see...

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.700
But...

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.410
...it's okay. My current performance
and my performance with you...

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:45.540
This isn't the last chance for her to hear it.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.450
--Yep!
--That's right!

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:51.250
Good morning, guys!

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.200
Good morning!

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.910
Are we all here?

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:56.080
We are!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.830
Miss Akira will join us later, right?

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.700
Yeah. Okay then, let's go.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.200
It'll take ten minutes to get
to the venue on foot.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.950
U-Um, excuse me!

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:10.120
This may not be the right place to give
these to you, but I'll do it while I can.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.000
What? What is it?

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.410
A-Actually, nothing. I'm sorr--

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:17.410
Jeez! Stop being so hesitant.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.410
--Hey!
--Can I open it? I'll open it, okay?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.830
Wai--

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.790
Are they... charms?

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:31.160
They're in the shape of a bridge!
And they have our names!

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.790
Did you make these for us, Hozy?!

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:39.040
U-Um... I-I-I'm sorry that they aren't
well made... Th-They look tacky, too.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:42.580
I-I caused you trouble
because of my family stuff.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:46.700
Well, actually, I made them wishing
that we could do our best today.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.410
Hozy...

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:51.000
This is amazing! I'm so happy! Thank you!

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.410
These are filled with lots of love!

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.950
We're definitely gonna be okay today!

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.410
Thank you!

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.870
Here's yours, Mr. Takinami.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.870
What? I've got one, too? Thanks.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.040
Hozuki. Did you poke your
fingers with the needle?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.500
I did, but my fingertips
are very hard now, so...

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:12.000
Oh, Chika? We need to
get going or we'll be late.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.870
What's the deal with him?
He didn't even say thanks.

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.870
Kudo. That's the wrong direction.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:20.580
Oh. He must be really happy.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.370
Looks like it.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:26.620
This might be the first time
someone's given him a charm.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:30.290
This is crazy. It's a charm just for me...

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.750
Don't ever show your face
in front of me again!

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:36.200
We can just use him when fights get bad.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.160
Shall we get going, too?

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.620
Hey, Granddad...

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.910
The koto club you created really is amazing!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:49.870
I wish these days could go on forever...

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:52.910
Komaki! Hurry up!

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:53.250
"Monthly Hogaku Days"
Komaki! Hurry up!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.660
"Monthly Hogaku Days"
We're gonna head out to the venue now!

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.410
"Koto for Beginners"
What? Please wait for me, Mr. Tsukaji!

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:59.410
"Koto: You can play it, too"
"History of Traditional Japanese Music"
What? Please wait for me, Mr. Tsukaji!

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:05.870
In any case, do I have to go today, too?

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:09.750
When I go to concerts, I fall asleep
in the middle without fail.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.330
So I think it'd be better if you go alone.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:14.870
Komaki!

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:17.120
Are you taking your job seriously?!

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.660
We publish a specialized magazine
on traditional Japanese music!

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:23.580
And you're one of its editors,
for God's sake! So act like one!

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.660
I got the job through my personal connections.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.160
It's not like I'm interested
in traditional Japanese music.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.950
I've heard enough!

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:36.160
Don't you think koto is kinda a tough subject?

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:39.950
Then today's work suits you very well.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.540
What?

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:44.450
It's Kanagawa's qualifier for nationals.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:47.870
Koto is tough? Difficult to approach?

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.620
This is way beyond that.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:53.950
Today a bunch of high school students
in their prime battle it out!

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:57.620
"Tetsuki taken by force"

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:03.370
Whoa... So they're all our rivals, huh?

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.540
As expected, there are so many girls...

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.910
A total of 14 schools, was it?

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.370
Yeah. And the number of schools
that can go to nationals...

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.790
...is one.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.040
Yeah.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:17.870
Ugh!

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:21.290
Long time no see. I'm glad to see you again.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:22.410
You...!

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.330
Oh? You don't remember me?

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:27.450
I made friends with you guys
at the music festival.

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:31.000
I don't recall becoming your friend! But...

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.450
How could I forget...?

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:36.120
You told me that my tones
were unrefined that time!

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:39.000
I found out later that you were
saying I sucked, you bastard!

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:39.830
Yeah.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:41.080
Don't "yeah" me!

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:44.290
Let me tell you something!
We're not the same as we were then!

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.410
We're definitely gonna win today!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:51.250
Kanzaki! You often disappear on me
when I look away for a second!

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.330
Everyone's looking for you over--

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.700
Whoa! Tokise High School!

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.910
Yeah, that's us, why?

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:02.000
Er... I'm sorry! Are you their advisor?

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:06.040
I'm Taishin Yamamoto.
I'm the advisor for Hakuto's koto club.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:08.120
I'm delighted to meet you!

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:12.250
Well, thank you. I'm Takinami,
Tokise's advisor.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:16.700
When I heard Tokise's performance on
the traditional music festival's DVD,

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:19.660
I was sooo moved!

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.660
What kind of guidance do you give them?!

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:24.910
Nothing really. It's all my students doing.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.410
Wow! That's a cool answer!

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:31.910
Unlike the music festival, Tokise performs
right after Hakuto today, right?

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.580
I'll be rushing to hear your
performance after ours is over!

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.000
Thank you.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.500
What? We're playing right after Hakuto?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.370
Yeah.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:43.080
Huh?! The heck?!
How come we didn't know?!

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.290
Why didn't you tell us, Suzu?!

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:49.750
We'd be the second to last performance.
That's all you told us!

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.000
What? Did I have to tell you that?

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.080
Does the order somehow
affect your performance?

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.330
Are you scared?

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.000
Oh... I guess maybe you are, huh?

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.370
--No way! Order doesn't matter!

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:02.540
--He's right!
--No way! Order doesn't matter!

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:03.450
Then no problem, right?

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.290
--You're damn right!
--Yeah!

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:07.830
What wonderful leadership!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:11.200
My students give a very
good performance, too.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.910
So please listen at the stage wings.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.950
Mr. Yamamoto! Mio!

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:20.250
Oh, excuse me, but we have to go now.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.660
See you later.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:23.540
Let's go, Kanzaki!

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:27.120
Hey...

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.080
I'm not gonna lose, either...

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:32.540
...for sure.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.330
Is she gonna come running?

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.160
Satowa!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:57.040
They're serious... Everyone is
seriously aiming for nationals.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.040
"Service Entrance"

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:01.500
Thank you very much!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.750
Hey, Granny.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:05.410
You'll stay and listen to our
performance today, right?

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.830
Actually, I have some business
to take care of after this.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:09.870
What...? I see...

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:13.660
But, well... I'll finish it quickly
and come back.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:18.080
You guys are already like my grandkids, so...

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:21.250
Chika, hurry up! The next school
will be coming in soon.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:22.830
Yeah.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.660
I still feel very upset about
not being able to have

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:32.040
my granddad hear my performance,

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.450
but I'm glad that I've got you.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:44.290
We'll... take you to nationals, too, Granny.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.330
Chika!

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:52.200
You guys are gonna be okay, for sure.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:54.660
Go play to your heart's content.

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.500
"Tuning Room"

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:07.950
Kazusa.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:09.620
Hozumi!

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:11.540
Are you doing okay?

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.330
Is there anything I can help with?

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:17.410
Ah, no, I'm okay. Thank you very much.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.160
It's just that I'm kinda
more nervous than usual

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.750
since we're playing early, the third in line.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.330
I see. That's just natural.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.790
When you perform, all we, the support
members, can do is root for you,

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:31.830
but we'll be sending you
our strong spiritual power!

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:43.080
Well then, if you need anything,
just let me know.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.500
Hozumi!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:48.830
Let's play together at nationals for sure!

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:51.700
Of course!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:02.700
Whoa... It's been a while since
the last time we were in a hall!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.120
This place is smaller than
the one at the music festival.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:08.120
The number of schools
performing is about half, too.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:10.830
It's starting.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:15.000
We are now commencing

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:22.660
the 32nd Kanagawa Qualifier for
Japan High School Music Competition.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:27.330
Oh, wow! They're all high
school students! They're so young!

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:32.080
But as I thought, it seems there are
very few boys. How disappointing.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.080
Only one school can go to nationals, right?

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:37.870
I wonder which school I wanna root for...

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:40.580
Mr. Tsukaji. Which school
do you think will win?

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.330
Don't make it sound so simple.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:46.870
I really do want to say that the one
who worked the hardest will win.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:50.540
But even if they worked hard,
there are always those who make mistakes

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:54.750
due to the nervousness and pressure
from performing during the competition.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:57.830
Chemistry with the judges
is a significant factor, too.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:59.000
Really?

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:00.950
It can't be helped since judges are human, too.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.040
"Koto Performer - Hisako Midoriyama"
"Shakuhachi Performer - Yoshiharu Wada"
"President of Ichiei University of Music - Kai Asahina"
It can't be helped since judges are human, too.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.250
"Koto Performer - Hisako Midoriyama"
"Shakuhachi Performer - Yoshiharu Wada"
"President of Ichiei University of Music - Kai Asahina"
Today's judges are...

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.910
There's an uptight person.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:11.790
Well, as usual, it's reasonable to think
that Himesaka will be first place.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:15.620
But the Kanto Traditional Japanese
Music Festival that I couldn't go see...

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:20.370
I'm curious about Hakuto,
who beat out Himesaka for first place.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.620
The music festival's DVD...

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.910
...was broken by Komaki
before I watched it. It really hurt!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.000
"Hozuki School"

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:31.040
The lesson took longer than I thought.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:33.250
I have to hurry to the venue.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:41.540
So she's still angry with me, huh?
Well, it's not surprising, I guess.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.830
"Satowa Hozuki"

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:51.040
Excuse me, Grand Master.

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.450
What is it?

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:57.500
I'm heading out to
the national qualifier.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:01.450
As I told you before,
Satowa will perform, too.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.830
I'm driving there, so if you'd like--

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:07.750
Why would I go? She's been excommunicated.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:11.950
I'm the grand master. It's improper
for me to go hear her performance.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:13.830
It's not improper...

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:17.450
...because you're her mother
before you're her teacher.

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:21.330
You think I can say that I'm her mother?

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.620
I had my own problems to deal with,

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.040
so I turned my eyes away from her feelings.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:32.200
I gave a look of contempt and strong
rejection to the scream from her heart.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:35.830
I don't even have the right to call myself
her mother, let alone go to hear her--

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:37.540
Grand Master.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.250
Forgive me!

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:40.660
What? Hey...

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.200
What're you doing, Akira?

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:46.870
I'm sorry, but I don't have time,
so I'm taking you by force!

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:50.040
I know this is none of my business
and I'm being selfish.

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:52.540
But... I'm so fed up...!

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.830
The shackles of the school.
The hardships in the past.

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.910
Being bound by them and watching...

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:59.870
...others be bound! I'm fed up with all of it!

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:01.750
What's the fuss?

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:04.660
--Hm? Akira. What're you doing this time?

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:07.290
--Good timing. Come with us, Grandmother.
--Hm? Akira. What're you doing this time?

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:08.120
What?

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:11.000
You should hear their performance, too!

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:16.040
A-Akira! You're being rough!

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:19.700
I just got my driver's license.
Please hold on tight!

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:22.870
"Program"

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.700
"Program"
"Kata..." "Kata..."?

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.750
"Kata kata"? What're you
trying to say, Kudo?

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:30.870
Well, I can't read the name of
the piece Hakuto is gonna play.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.200
"Katakago"

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:34.080
"Katakago"
Yeah. I wonder what it is... "Katagashi"?

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.790
"Katakago." It's the name of a flower.
If I remember correctly,

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:39.080
it's an archaic word for <i>katakuri.</i>

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:41.870
Even the name sounds difficult.

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:44.160
Do you think it's another original piece?

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:48.330
Most likely. The same composer wrote it.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.160
Let's see...

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:52.500
"Composed by Miyabi Tojo"
The composer is Miyabi Tojo.

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:54.370
Have you heard of the person?

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:58.540
No. I checked,
but I couldn't find anything.

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:02.790
It looks like Hakuto's got
a very good composer.

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:03.580
"Program"

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.580
Hozuki. Why are you so quiet?

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.500
Well, Himesaka is...

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.040
Himesaka?

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.950
I was thinking they're playing
another difficult piece.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.250
Everyone, it's about time.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.500
Club President.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.290
Yes.

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:20.700
Everyone. We're finally at the qualifier.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:24.330
We really went through a lot to get here.

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:27.290
We argued and fought the most this time,

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:30.120
and the mood was often bad, to be honest.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:32.580
There are also members
who can't perform today.

00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:37.250
But they helped the performing
members a lot as support members.

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:41.200
All of us were needed to come here today.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:44.250
As the club president, I can proudly say...

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:47.790
...that we've practiced more
than any other school.

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:50.620
We'll win today with everyone here together!

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:52.620
Form a circle!

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:55.040
We are one!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:58.080
We're the champions of Kanagawa!

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.540
Let's go!

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:52.660
Next time, "Champions' Resolve."

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.540
"#23    Champions' Resolve"
